       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. At that dose, the risks of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects go up. Higher doses haven't been shown to work better.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n- **The dose was a typo.** Common intended doses are 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily. For depression or anxiety, the usual start is 25\u201350 mg daily, titrated up in 25\u201350 mg steps no more often than weekly.\n- **The dose is intentional.** Some specialists go above 200 mg for refractory cases. If that's your plan, tell me and add a note with the rationale, such as psychiatry's recommendation. I can enter it with that note, though pharmacy may still ask you to verify it.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter? If you want a different dose, give me the number. I'll also need the indication if you'd like it in the order note."
